{"id": "tea:nacciyar-tirumoli:1", "source": "src:nacciyar-tirumoli", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Āṇṭāḷ prays to Kāma, god of love, to unite her with the Lord of Vēṅkaṭam: if she is spoken of as destined for a mortal man, she will not live.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "consciousness-mind"], "speaker": "Āṇṭāḷ", "teachers": ["tch:andal"], "concepts": ["cpt:nayika-bhava"], "terms": ["trm:kanta-bhava"], "notes": "Decad-level; 'māṉiṭavarkku eṉṟu pēccup paṭil vāḻkillēṉ' recalled as in this decad (verse 5).", "coverage": ["A9"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "translation_basis": "skeleton paraphrase from model knowledge of the text; not made from an edition", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nacciyar-tirumoli:12-13", "source": "src:nacciyar-tirumoli", "location": {"ref": "12-13"}, "paraphrase": "In the agony of separation she asks to be taken to Mathurā, Gokula, the Yamunā bank, and begs for his garment, his tulasī garland or the breeze from him to cool her burning.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "powers-experiences"], "speaker": "Āṇṭāḷ", "teachers": ["tch:andal"], "concepts": ["cpt:viraha-bhakti", "cpt:signs-of-the-lover-of-god"], "notes": "Decad-range summary recalled generally; decad numbers low confidence.", "coverage": ["A9"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "translation_basis": "skeleton paraphrase from model knowledge of the text; not made from an edition", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nacciyar-tirumoli:14", "source": "src:nacciyar-tirumoli", "location": {"ref": "14"}, "paraphrase": "'Have you seen him?' — 'We saw him in Vṛndāvana': the closing decad, in which the girls report the sight of the Lord in his glory.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "speaker": "Āṇṭāḷ", "teachers": ["tch:andal"], "concepts": ["cpt:nayika-bhava"], "notes": "'paṭṭi mēyntōr kāreṟu'. Decad-level.", "coverage": ["A9"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "translation_basis": "skeleton paraphrase from model knowledge of the text; not made from an edition", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nacciyar-tirumoli:6", "source": "src:nacciyar-tirumoli", "location": {"ref": "6"}, "paraphrase": "'I dreamed, my friend': the elephant procession, the canopy, the Lord's coming as bridegroom, the rites of the wedding, the hand taken and the steps round the fire — her marriage to the Lord seen in a dream.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "speaker": "Āṇṭāḷ", "teachers": ["tch:andal"], "concepts": ["cpt:nayika-bhava"], "notes": "'vāraṇam āyiram'; sung at Śrīvaiṣṇava weddings.", "coverage": ["A9"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "translation_basis": "skeleton paraphrase from model knowledge of the text; not made from an edition", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nacciyar-tirumoli:7", "source": "src:nacciyar-tirumoli", "location": {"ref": "7"}, "paraphrase": "She asks the white conch Pāñcajanya, which touches the Lord's lips: do they smell of camphor, of the lotus? are those coral lips sweet? — envying the conch its nearness.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "speaker": "Āṇṭāḷ", "teachers": ["tch:andal"], "concepts": ["cpt:nayika-bhava", "cpt:viraha-bhakti"], "notes": "'karpūram nāṟumō'.", "coverage": ["A9"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "translation_basis": "skeleton paraphrase from model knowledge of the text; not made from an edition", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U25-alvar-bhakti-theory"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
